WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.720
It seems like the appetite for&nbsp;
sequels will never be satisfied,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:08.700
and Hollywood is happy to provide as many&nbsp;
retreads, revivals, and follow-ups as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:16.334
audiences want. From obscure prequels to mega&nbsp;
sequels, 2024 is filled with familiar stories.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:22.500
While the nearly silent A Quiet Place stays&nbsp;
entirely focused on one small family headed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.580
by parents played by Emily Blunt and John&nbsp;
Krasinski, who also co-wrote the script&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:31.500
and served as director, the sequel,&nbsp;
A Quiet Place Part II zooms out. That&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.520
film brings the surviving characters from&nbsp;
the first film into contact with a small,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:39.300
peaceful community that's managed to&nbsp;
stay isolated from the sound-seeking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:44.760
monstrosities prowling the world around them.&nbsp;
Now a third A Quiet Place film is on the docket.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:49.920
Pig writer-director Michael Sarnoski will&nbsp;
oversee A Quiet Place: Day One. And word&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:54.660
has it that Blunt and Krasinski won't appear.&nbsp;
Instead, the leads will be played by Lupita&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:59.100
Nyong'o and Joseph Quinn of Stranger Things&nbsp;
fame. We don't know much about the plot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:04.534
but we do know that A Quiet Place: Day&nbsp;
One will be released on March 8, 2024.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:10.440
The Kung Fu Panda franchise combined some&nbsp;
potentially ill-fitting pieces — martial arts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:16.740
talking animals, an ancient setting, comedy, and&nbsp;
action — but in terms of acclaim and box office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:22.140
the gambit worked. In the original Kung&nbsp;
Fu Panda from 2008, Jack Black voiced Po,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:27.720
an energetic panda in a fantastical ancient&nbsp;
China where animals rule and people don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:34.010
exist. Po is selected as the chosen one, a&nbsp;
kung fu master known as the Dragon Warrior.

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:34.801
"You."

00:01:34.801 --> 00:01:35.580
"Me?"

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:41.775
"The universe has brought us the Dragon Warrior."

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:46.680
He trains under a red panda,&nbsp;
Master Shifu, learns to be a hero,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:51.660
and teams up with other animals to fight a&nbsp;
bunch of bad guys in the film's two sequels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:57.240
released in 2011 and 2016, to complete&nbsp;
the trilogy. Or so everyone thought.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:04.260
But the Kung Fu Panda movies brought in $1.8&nbsp;
billion at the box office. And three spinoff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:09.780
TV shows plus multiple animated specials proved&nbsp;
an enduring interest in the brand, prompting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:15.180
DreamWorks Animation to consider a revival. Plot&nbsp;
details are scant, but we suspect that original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:22.020
voice actors Black, Dustin Hoffman, Jackie Chan,&nbsp;
Lucy Liu, David Cross, Angelina Jolie, and Seth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:28.608
Rogan will reprise their roles. Kung Fu Panda&nbsp;
4 arrives in movie theaters on March 8, 2024.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:36.540
Let's get ready to rumble – again! Everybody's&nbsp;
favorite Titans — Godzilla and King Kong — are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:41.460
in training for their rematch. The first&nbsp;
film hit theaters and HBO Max in 2021,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:48.240
earning $468 million and impressing critics. Adam&nbsp;
Wingard is returning to direct, and this time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:52.140
he's teaming up with an old friend, Dan&nbsp;
Stevens, who'll be playing the lead.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:57.480
Stevens and Wingard previously worked together on&nbsp;
the horror classic The Guest. If you haven't seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:01.800
it, you probably know Stevens from projects&nbsp;
like Downton Abbey, Beauty and the Beast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:06.420
and Legion. He'll be joined by MonsterVerse&nbsp;
veterans Rebecca Hall, Brian Tyree Henry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:11.640
and Kaylee Hottle, along with newcomers&nbsp;
Rachel House, Fala Chen, and Alex Ferns.

00:03:11.845 --> 00:03:16.285
"Okay, but when it comes&nbsp;
to Kong, what I say goes."

00:03:16.285 --> 00:03:20.640
The script is being penned by longtime&nbsp;
Wingard collaborator Simon Barrett,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:26.280
Jeremy Slater of Moon Knight, and Terry Rossio&nbsp;
of Pirates of the Caribbean fame. The new feature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:31.680
has the two famous screen monsters teaming&nbsp;
up again to fight a new hidden threat that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:36.180
is bent on destroying the world. It also dives&nbsp;
into the histories of the two characters and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:41.100
reveals what created these creatures, and&nbsp;
why they are eternally linked to humanity.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:45.180
In the original film, they teamed up to&nbsp;
take out Mechagodzilla. This time around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:49.560
will they throw down against&nbsp;
Mechani-Kong? Space Godzilla&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:53.770
perhaps? Whatever ends up happening,&nbsp;
we're excited for the showdown.

00:03:53.770 --> 00:04:01.620
In 2015, Mad Max: Fury Road reinvigorated the&nbsp;
Mad Max franchise, which began in 1979 with Mel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:06.480
Gibson in the title role. Fury Road offered&nbsp;
a fresh spin on the post-apocalyptic tale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:13.200
shifting focus to Charlize Theron's rage-fueled&nbsp;
Imperator Furiosa. Mad Max: Fury Road wowed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:19.140
audiences and critics alike, with many considering&nbsp;
it one of the best action films of all time.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:24.660
Now there's a Fury Road prequel in the works.&nbsp;
Titled Furiosa, it brings back the title&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:29.220
character, although Theron won't be appearing&nbsp;
in the film. Director George Miller said that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:32.700
much as he loved Theron's performance&nbsp;
in Fury Road, he doesn't have enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:36.360
faith in de-aging technology to have&nbsp;
her reprise her role in the prequel.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:42.000
Instead, the younger Furiosa will be played&nbsp;
by Anya Taylor-Joy. She'll be joined by MCU&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:46.200
star Chris Hemsworth and Tom Burke of&nbsp;
Mank. The movie will tell the tale of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:50.880
how Furiosa came to be stolen from the Green&nbsp;
Place of Many Mothers and wound up in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:54.960
hands of the Great Biker Horde and their&nbsp;
leader Dementus. The main conflict of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:59.340
story revolves around the war that breaks out&nbsp;
when Dementus finds Immortan Joe's Citadel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:04.380
Furiosa has to survive the conflict as she&nbsp;
desperately tries to find a way to get home.

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:09.600
A fourth entry in the rebooted Planet of&nbsp;
the Apes franchise is on the way from Maze&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:14.400
Runner director Wes Ball and screenwriter Josh&nbsp;
Friedman. In 2020, Ball tweeted that the new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:19.067
film would continue the legacy of Caesar, the&nbsp;
leader of the apes in the first three films.

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:21.991
"Take your stinking paw off&nbsp;
me, you damn dirty ape!"

00:05:24.832 --> 00:05:27.101
"No!"

00:05:27.101 --> 00:05:33.180
But Caesar ended the third movie mortally wounded,&nbsp;
leading to speculation that Ball was referring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:38.700
to Caesar's son, Cornelius. Further news on the&nbsp;
project came in August 2022, when it was announced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:44.220
that Owen Teague will play the lead primate. He'll&nbsp;
be joined by costars Freya Allan, Peter Macon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:50.820
and William H. Macy. Amanda Silver and Rick Jaffa&nbsp;
— who wrote Rise and Dawn of the Planet of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:55.080
Apes — are back for the fourth installment.&nbsp;
In an interview with FilmSpeak, they teased,

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:08.520
After bringing children's playthings to life&nbsp;
with the Toy Story films and inviting viewers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:14.580
into the secret worlds of fish, monsters, and&nbsp;
superheroes with Finding Nemo, Monsters, Inc.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:20.640
and The Incredibles, Pixar gave us Inside&nbsp;
Out in 2015. The film explored the triumphs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:25.740
and agonies of adolescence, as experienced&nbsp;
through the eyes of a kid named Riley and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:30.480
personified emotions that live inside her head.&nbsp;
The film won best animated feature at the Academy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:36.840
Awards and took in $857 million, prompting&nbsp;
Disney to put Pixar to work on a sequel.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:41.760
Kelsey Mann, a Pixar veteran who co-wrote&nbsp;
The Good Dinosaur, will direct Inside Out 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:45.360
and Inside Out screenwriter Meg&nbsp;
LeFauve will write the script. Sadly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:50.287
we know for a fact that Mindy Kaling&nbsp;
will not reprise her role of Disgust.

00:06:50.287 --> 00:06:53.227
"Riley is acting so weird.&nbsp;
Why is she acting so weird?"

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:58.680
As for the plot, Riley is now a teenager, which&nbsp;
means there will likely be some new characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:04.429
taking up residence in her head. Inside&nbsp;
Out 2 lands in theaters on June 14, 2024.

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:10.680
In January 2019, Mission: Impossible franchise&nbsp;
creative leader Christopher McQuarrie announced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:15.780
that the seventh and eighth installments in&nbsp;
the enduring action-spy franchise would film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:21.000
consecutively. But then delays brought on by&nbsp;
the COVID-19 pandemic — and with it, Cruise's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:25.620
contractual obligations to promote Top Gun:&nbsp;
Maverick — pushed everything back. As Dead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:30.120
Reckoning Part One is now scheduled for&nbsp;
theatrical release in the summer of 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:33.780
its immediate sequel — and the&nbsp;
eighth entry in the Mission:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:39.540
Impossible series overall — has been pushed back.
Details of the follow-up are under wraps. But we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:43.860
know there will be a stunt involving&nbsp;
a biplane 2,000 feet up in the air,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:50.234
with Tom Cruise actually standing on the thing&nbsp;
instead of sitting in it like a normal person.

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:55.560
Even before the release of the Despicable&nbsp;
Me spinoff feature Minions: The Rise of Gru,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.560 --> 00:08:00.180
Universal is looking ahead to the next&nbsp;
installment of the main franchise. Despicable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:06.780
Me 4 is slated to hit theaters on July 3, 2024.&nbsp;
The animated Despicable Me films center around a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:12.060
reformed supervillain named Gru, voiced by&nbsp;
a heavily accented Steve Carell who leaves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:17.580
his dastardly ways behind after adopting a trio&nbsp;
of adorable daughters and discovering the joys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:22.020
frustrations, and responsibilities&nbsp;
of parenthood. Aided by his troupe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:27.000
of gibberish-spouting yellow Minions, Gru&nbsp;
has spent each Despicable Me film venturing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:30.540
into unfamiliar territory to make the&nbsp;
world a safer place for his family.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:37.620
Along with Carell, returning for Despicable Me 4&nbsp;
are Kristen Wiig, Pierre Coffin, Miranda Cosgrove,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:42.030
and Steve Coogan, along with director Chris&nbsp;
Renaud, who helmed the first two films. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:45.960
will be joined by co-director Patrick&nbsp;
Delage, who directed both Sing movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:51.540
and the duo will be working off a script by School&nbsp;
of Rock scribe Mike White. While we don't yet know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:57.960
the plot for Despicable Me 4, we can only imagine&nbsp;
it will once again see Gru face off against a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:03.420
scheming villain to save the world, even though he&nbsp;
admires their diabolical plan just a little bit.

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:09.420
After the massive commercial success of Disney's&nbsp;
photo-realistic remake of The Lion King,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:12.960
it seemed like only a matter of time&nbsp;
before a sequel was announced. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:18.600
the person taking over the directorial reins from&nbsp;
Jon Favreau for Lion King 2 — now titled Mufasa:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:22.560
The Lion King — is probably not a name&nbsp;
most people would have expected to hear:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:28.020
Barry Jenkins, the Academy Award-winning writer&nbsp;
and director best known for making poignant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:32.640
dramas with strong racial themes, including&nbsp;
Moonlight and If Beale Street Could Talk.

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:36.900
Jenkins will be working from a script by&nbsp;
Jeff Nathanson, who also wrote the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:41.400
Lion King. While no specific details of the&nbsp;
plot have been revealed, we know the film will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:45.834
be a prequel to the first film, following&nbsp;
Mufasa and Scar in their younger years.

00:09:45.834 --> 00:09:48.654
"Well, look who's come down&nbsp;
to mingle with the commoners."

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:55.920
It will also introduce several new characters.&nbsp;
However, no further information has been provided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.920 --> 00:10:00.660
about these characters, including what types of&nbsp;
animals they are or whose side they might be on.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:04.560
Although Lion King seems like an&nbsp;
outlier in Jenkins' filmography,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:07.920
the director sounds excited about&nbsp;
working on the sequel for Disney, saying,

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:26.040
In 1996, Twister stormed its way&nbsp;
to blockbuster status, offering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:31.980
an irresistible combination of fantastic&nbsp;
actors, romantic tension, science jargon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:36.540
and a frightening villain: the weather.&nbsp;
Directed by action movie stalwart Jan de Bont,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:41.460
Twister depicts a team of university scientists&nbsp;
led by Dr. Jo Harding, played by Helen Hunt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:45.960
as they try to put a data-gathering device to&nbsp;
work during an onslaught of tornadoes. She's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:50.640
forced to team up with her ex-husband, played&nbsp;
by Bill Paxton, to get everything operational,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:56.100
especially when their sneering rival Dr. Jonas&nbsp;
Miller plans to use a device he built himself.

00:10:56.100 --> 00:11:03.180
Twister picked up $241.7 million at the&nbsp;
box office, so a sequel makes sense. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:07.620
just took a long time for all the necessary&nbsp;
pieces to come together. In October 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:11.400
Deadline reported that legendary&nbsp;
filmmaker and Amblin Entertainment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:16.380
boss Steven Spielberg loved a script written&nbsp;
by Mark L. Smith, best known for The Revenant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:20.820
and put the film into pre-production. After Top&nbsp;
Gun: Maverick director Joseph Kosinski dropped out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:25.440
due to a scheduling conflict, it was reported&nbsp;
that Lee Isaac Chung of Minari fame will direct.

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:29.940
Producers are hoping to sign Helen Hunt, as&nbsp;
the plot of the sequel — currently titled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:33.960
Twisters — will emphasize her relationship with&nbsp;
her daughter, whose father was the character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:41.340
portrayed by Paxton, who died in 2017. The&nbsp;
film will roar into theaters on July 19, 2024.

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:48.000
2019's Joker takes a daring new approach&nbsp;
to Batman's most famous adversary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:54.840
as inspired by gritty '70s cinema as it is by&nbsp;
comic books. Joaquin Phoenix plays Arthur Fleck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:59.220
a troubled wannabe comedian who suffers an&nbsp;
emotional breakdown on the way to becoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:04.140
the clownish supervillain. Joker earned&nbsp;
more than $1 billion at the box office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:08.520
and Phoenix took home the Best Actor&nbsp;
Oscar for his work in the film. Clearly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:13.740
there's demand for additional movies&nbsp;
about this Joker's rise to infamy.

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:18.180
According to The Hollywood Reporter, director&nbsp;
Todd Phillips discussed tackling more DC Comics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:24.060
movies mere days after Joker debuted. In June&nbsp;
2022, Phillips confirmed rumors of a sequel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:28.740
when he posted a photo of the next Joker&nbsp;
script to Instagram. The snapshot revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:33.240
that the film will be titled Joker: Folie&nbsp;
à Deux. "Folie à deux" is a psychological&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:39.240
term referring to a delusion shared by multiple&nbsp;
people, which suggests a tantalizing team-up.

00:12:39.465 --> 00:12:45.539
"Arthur, you're on seven different medications.&nbsp;
Surely they must be doing something."

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:51.180
As it turns out, Phoenix will return&nbsp;
in the title role, alongside Lady Gaga&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:57.600
as Harley Quinn. And in a fascinating twist,&nbsp;
the new film will be a musical set in Arkham&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:02.580
Asylum. Providing at least some of the musical&nbsp;
content will be composer Hildur Guðnadóttir,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:05.940
who won an Academy Award for&nbsp;
scoring the first Joker film.

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:10.620
As for the rest of the cast, Phoenix and&nbsp;
Gaga will be joined by Brendan Gleeson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:14.280
Catherine Keener, and returning Joker actor Zazie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:19.420
Beetz. The film will dance its way&nbsp;
into theaters on October 4, 2024.

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:25.440
An allegory about environmentalism&nbsp;
and imperialism, Avatar was a visually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:30.060
stunning experience. Set in the distant&nbsp;
future on the idyllic planet of Pandora,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:35.040
the film saw an Earth-based contingent&nbsp;
seeking a rare substance and interacting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:38.760
with the indigenous, blue-skinned&nbsp;
Na'vi. In the middle of all this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:43.680
paralyzed former Marine Jake Sully fully&nbsp;
embraced the Na'vi culture by way of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:48.360
mental link-up with his avatar, a genetically&nbsp;
modified Na'vi body that shares his DNA.

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:52.440
"It'd be a fresh start in&nbsp;
a new world. You could do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:55.627
something important. You could make a difference."

00:13:55.800 --> 00:14:02.760
In 2009 and 2010, Avatar became a worldwide&nbsp;
pop culture sensation and the highest-grossing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:07.380
movie ever made. Writer-director James&nbsp;
Cameron announced weeks after the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:11.580
film hit theaters that he was working&nbsp;
on a sequel, and, by the end of 2010,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:18.540
Cameron promised a third Avatar. By 2015, those&nbsp;
plans had ballooned into a five-film series.

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:24.660
Of course, such complicated movies take a lot of&nbsp;
money and time to realize, and the aquatics-heavy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:31.080
Avatar: The Way of Water hit theaters 13 years&nbsp;
after the original. But audiences packed theaters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:38.040
as they had for the first film, to the tune of&nbsp;
$1.9 billion in ticket sales. In the wake of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:42.780
the first sequel's success, Cameron has dropped&nbsp;
some details about Avatar 3, telling Deadline,

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:57.600
Evidently, the fire nation will be a bit&nbsp;
different from your normal Na'vi. Led by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:01.440
Oona Chaplin from Game of Thrones,&nbsp;
the so-called "Ash People" will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:04.620
a villainous bunch. Cameron told&nbsp;
the French news outlet 20 Minutes,

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:24.480
We also know that instead of Jake Sully doing&nbsp;
voiceover, Avatar 3 will be narrated by his son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:29.940
Lo'ak. And we can also expect to see the&nbsp;
return of Payakan the tulkun and Scoresby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:34.860
the whaler. So far, word is the movie will&nbsp;
officially be called Avatar: The Seed Bearer.

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:39.000
The third Avatar opens on December 20, 2024.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:45.120
After the initial trailer sparked revulsion&nbsp;
from fans and necessitated a hasty redesign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:48.900
by the studio thanks to a bizarrely&nbsp;
rendered version of Sonic the Hedgehog,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:53.100
the first film to feature the character&nbsp;
managed to win crowds over at the box office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:59.220
and earn itself a sequel. Yet before Sonic the&nbsp;
Hedgehog 2 zoomed onto screens in April 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:03.780
a third film had already been greenlit by&nbsp;
Paramount, which will once again bring together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:09.000
Ben Schwartz as the voice of the titular&nbsp;
hedgehog and James Marsden as his endlessly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:13.980
patient and forgiving human best bud Tom, along&nbsp;
with Jim Carrey as the villainous Dr. Robotnik.

00:16:13.980 --> 00:16:18.060
Considering that Sonic the Hedgehog 2 hadn't&nbsp;
hit theaters when the threequel was announced,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:22.020
plot details about the third film are&nbsp;
still sparse. However, considering that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:26.580
Paramount and Sega have announced a spinoff&nbsp;
television series centered around Knuckles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:31.500
a new character introduced in the second movie and&nbsp;
voiced by Idris Elba, we wouldn't be surprised if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:37.080
Knuckles also shows up in a third Sonic, along&nbsp;
with Sonic's new sidekick Tails, Tom's wife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:42.540
Maddie, and Maddie's scene-stealing sister,&nbsp;
Rachel. Much like the blue hedgehog himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:49.086
Paramount is moving fast: Sonic the Hedgehog&nbsp;
3 will speed into theaters December 20, 2024.

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:53.820
In his Great Movie review, Roger Ebert hailed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:57.720
original This Is Spinal Tap as "one&nbsp;
of the funniest movies ever made."

00:16:57.720 --> 00:17:04.440
"It's very, very special, because, if you&nbsp;
can see, yeah, the numbers all go to 11."

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:10.860
The 1984 mockumentary tells the story of fading&nbsp;
band Spinal Tap, desperately searching for musical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:15.180
glory in a world that's forgotten them. And&nbsp;
the whole time, they're being filmed by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:20.340
not-so-talented documentarian Marty DiBergi —&nbsp;
played by the film's actual director, Rob Reiner.

00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:26.100
With its so-terrible-they're-amazing songs&nbsp;
and improvised jokes, it's no wonder that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:30.000
This Is Spinal Tap became an instant&nbsp;
classic. And now, Reiner is getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:35.340
the band back together. Original stars Michael&nbsp;
McKean, Christopher Guest, and Harry Shearer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:40.020
will be picking up their guitars and rocking&nbsp;
'round Stonehenge in the film's upcoming sequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:46.380
scheduled for release in 2024 — right in time&nbsp;
for the original's 40th anniversary. Reiner will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:51.720
return as both the film's director and DiBergi.&nbsp;
Here's hoping they can turn this sequel up to 11.

